<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Debug-only. Merges into the debug APK and **never** into the release one, and it
  is not `src/main/AndroidManifest.xml` — which is the manifest
  `manifest-hardening`, `OpenExternallyScanTest` and `LauncherIdentityScanTest`
  read, and which is unchanged by this file.

  It carries two things, and both are debug-only for the same reason: neither belongs in an APK
  that is uploaded.

  **One — the crash log's `Application`** (`debug-crash-log`). `android:name` is overridden to
  `DebugVaultApplication`, which extends the shipped `VaultApplication`, installs
  `DebugCrashLog` and does nothing else. The override is what keeps the handler out of `main`:
  `OUTLINE.md` I2 forbids crash-reporting SDKs, and a class that is not in the release APK is a
  stronger claim than a class that ships and is branched around by `BuildConfig.DEBUG`.
  `tools:replace` is required — the merger treats two `android:name` values on `<application>` as a
  conflict and fails the build rather than picking one.

  **Two — a host activity for Compose tests.** A Compose test needs a host activity to call
  setContent on, and that activity must live in the app under test's process —
  an activity declared in the androidTest manifest belongs to
  com.app.vault.test and ActivityScenario refuses to launch it. The usual
  supplier is androidx.compose.ui:ui-test-manifest, a debugImplementation that
  declares exactly this; P2-23's block adds no Gradle dependency, so the
  declaration is written out here instead. It is the same component either way.

  **Not MainActivity.** AppearanceDeviceTest originally hosted its compositions in
  the real activity, whose onCreate loads the index, connects Billing and reads
  the biometric wrap. Launching it twenty times per run left a Keystore alias
  behind and made BiometricWrapTest's "creation must touch no Keystore alias"
  fail — a test that passed alone and failed in the suite, which is the worst
  kind. A bare ComponentActivity runs none of our code.

  Not exported, and carrying no intent filter: nothing but the instrumentation
  ever starts it, and it is not a launcher entry.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
    <application
        android:name=".DebugVaultApplication"
        tools:replace="android:name">
        <activity
            android:name="androidx.activity.ComponentActivity"
            android:exported="false" />
    </application>
</manifest>
